Scan deadline regression tests
==============================

From the kernel source directory:

  ./tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run \
    --kunitconfig=drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/tests \
    'brcmfmac-scan-timeout*'

These hardware-independent tests cover the 10-second floor, the 97-channel
passive-scan regression (24,280 ms budget), active requests with potentially
passive channels, the 60-second ceiling, overflow and all-band fallback.
They do not simulate firmware completion, timer cancellation or association.

The regular v1-v4 request builders use -1 dwell values; the timeout uses the
120 ms passive default programmed by brcmf_dongle_scantime(). They currently
do not implement cfg80211 request duration overrides. The extra per-channel
dwell and one-second allowance are a conservative watchdog policy, not a
measured upper bound on every firmware implementation. P2P retains its
existing timeout because it overrides the regular scan's dwell policy.

Internal PNO follow-up scans call brcmf_do_escan() directly and do not arm the
foreground timeout timer. This change intentionally leaves that lifecycle,
foreground completion/abort cleanup and scan-parameter version negotiation
unchanged. Every foreground request computes a fresh deadline before starting
firmware work; no request pointer is retained by the deadline helper.

Hardware acceptance still requires the identical full passive request to
complete with fresh results, full/single-channel active and passive scans,
explicit abort followed by retry, and ordinary all-band supplicant scanning.
Keep independent network access while isolating the supplicant. A larger iw
userspace timeout does not change the kernel deadline. Check scan events, not
only cached BSS entries. Test association and traffic separately.
